$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General procedure A for the synthesis of substrate (1): 1 To a Schlenk
tube (50-mL) were added Pd(PPh3)2Cl2 (70 mg, 0.1 mmol, 2 mol %),
K3PO4·nH2O (1.73 g, 7.5 mmol, 1.5 equiv) and substrate 3 (5 mmol, 1.0
equiv). The mixture was closed by a septum, purged by nitrogen gas for
several times then the dry toluene (20 mL) was slowly injected into the
mixture by a syringe and the mixture was allowed to stir for 10 min;
o-bromoiodoarene 4 (7.5 mmol) was then slowly injected into the mixture
by a syringe. The septum was removed and the Schlenk tube was sealed with
cap; again quickly purged by nitrogen gas for several times and move to
oil bath and allowed to stir at 100 °C for 12 h. The crude reaction
mixture was diluted with 30 mL CH2Cl2, filtered through a thin Celite pad
to remove salt and concentrated in vacuo. The residue was isolated
through column chromatography by using hexane and ethyl acetate as
eluent. Compounds 1. Compounds 1a–1o, 1A–1F and 1H–1J were obtained
according to this procedure. 2'-Bromo-[1,1'-biphenyl]-2-carbonitrile
(1a): According to the general procedure A, Pd(PPh3)2Cl2 (70 mg, 0.1
mmol, 2 mol %), K3PO4·nH2O (1.73 g, 7.5 mmol, 1.5 equiv),
2-(4,4,5,5-tetramethyl- 1,3,2-dioxaborolan-2-yl)benzonitrile (1.15 g, 5
mmol, 1.0 equiv) and o-bromoiodobenzene (1.69 g, 6.0 mmol, 1.2 equiv)
were stirred in dry toluene (20 mL) at 100 °C for 2 h. Work-up and
purification by column chromatography (Hex/EtOAc = 19:1). Product 1a as a
white solid (1.14 g, 88%). Registry Number: [54245-41-9]. mp: 66–67 °C;
IR (KBr): 3064, 2230, 1601, 811, 763 cm-1; 1H NMR (600 MHz, CDCl3): δ
7.77 (dd, J = 7.8, 0.6 Hz, 1H), 7.72 (dd, J = 8.4, 0.6 Hz, 1H), 7.66 (td,
J = 7.8, 1.2 Hz, 1H), 7.50 (td, J = 7.8, 1.2 Hz, 1H), 7.44–7.41 (m, 2H),
7.35–7.30 (m, 2H); 13C NMR (150 MHz, CDCl3): δ 144.7, 139.0, 133.1,
132.8, 132.3, 130.9, 130.7, 130.3, 128.2, 127.5, 122.8, 117.7, 112.9;
HRMS (EI+): 256.9837 (cal. for C13H8BrN 256.9840)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM chemoselective, slow additions of toluene stage 1 and arene stage 2,
sealed tube used (Schlenk), Suzuki coupling
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Hydride-Induced Anionic Cyclization: An Efficient Method for the
Synthesis of 6-H-Phenanthridines via a Transition-Metal-Free Process
